A toolchain should get a last chance to do something right before a build/clean gets started.

It should be possible to:
 - Adjust tool options before build - based on external data, for example.
 - Reject the build if there is something wrong: The tool chain could create its own error markers and the build will be silently stopped. 
 - Throw an exception if there is something seriously wrong: CoreException

I think this could be implemented quite easily adding a handler to the tool chain definition.

interface IBuildLastChance {
 public boolean performLastChance(int buildKind, IConfiguration config, ...) throws CoreException;
}

The method returns false if the build should be rejected.

